# Kit, without any claim (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Claims in someone else's kit"): people react to what
# you wear. Your own colours suit you; theirs on a stranger get a question, never an accusation.
# There's no disguise with the Haven (its mark is the bear on its doors, not on its people).

conv named.bastion.kit_own
for named:bastion
when kit:own
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say "Kit suits you. Mind the collar. The sergeant notices collars."

conv named.bastion.kit_theirs
for named:bastion
when kit:in_kit & !passing
greet
voice bastion
daily

node start
  say "Where did you get that jacket? Don't answer. I'd have to write it down."

conv named.redhand.kit_own
for named:redhand
when kit:own
greet
voice redhand
daily

node start
  say "Wearing the red. Good. Now everyone knows who to blame."

conv named.redhand.kit_theirs
for named:redhand
when kit:in_kit & !passing
greet
voice redhand
daily

node start
  say "Nice armband. Whose was it before? Doesn't matter. Everything was somebody's before."

conv named.halcyon.kit_theirs
for named:halcyon
when kit:in_kit & !passing
greet
voice halcyon
daily

node start
  say "That coat has somebody's initials in the collar. They aren't yours."
